Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 10/25/2024]
1. Er = 1012 - 4327 keV: we used the same directly measured resonance strengths as in Iliadis et al. 2010; those values had been adopted from Smulders & Endt 1962; 
   Lyons et al. 1969; Maas et al. 1978; Cseh et al. 1982; Strandberg et al. 2008.
2. Er = 200, 291, 329, 962 keV: Gg = 0.5 eV is an inconsequential guess; Ga upper limit is equal to the Wigner limit.
3. Er = 208 keV: the (6Li,d) angular distribution in Tanabe et al. 1983 for Ex = 10.19 keV is fitted with ell = 5.
4. For these pairs of levels, it is not clear which level of each pair corresponds to the peaks observed in the (6Li,d) spectrum of Tanabe et al. 1983 [Fig. 2]:
   Er = 532 + 559 keV; 687 + 824 keV; 934 + 971 keV. In these cases, we sample for each pair discretely with 50% probability. 
5. The radius parameter of r0 = 0.84 fm was chosen to be consistent with the bound state parameters in the (6Li,d) analysis of S_a in Tanabe et al. 1983.
6. Direct capture (E2) is estimated using (adopting) alpha spectroscopic factors from (6Li,d) experiment of Tanabe et al. 1983.
